{"step_index":5674,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T19:46:18Z","thinking":"Ambiguous candidates, identified by brand similarity (60-85%) and compatible strength, are directed to an LLM for review. Upon an LLM \"match\" response, further validation is performed on strength, combination, brand similarity (>=65%), and form. A form mismatch results in \"review\" status; otherwise, \"match\" status is retained. A \"review\" response from the LLM directly sets the status to \"review.\"\n\n\nWhen the LLM rejects all ambiguous candidates, the system checks for a previously identified \"review candidate\" (same brand, strength, but different form). This \"review candidate\" would be used if the LLM's \"no_match\" implies that only the form is different. Alternatively, if `classify_pair` identifies the top candidate as requiring review (due to a form difference), it is correctly marked for review. This logic ensures no valid form discrepancies are missed.\n\n\nA high brand similarity (>= 80%) with no other conflicts triggers a \"needs_review\" status even if the initial status is \"no_match,\" preventing potential matches from being incorrectly discarded. The \"needs_review\" status is assigned when there is a significant brand connection but potential discrepancies that require pharmacist oversight. It captures cases with high brand similarity, but potential differences in form, strength, or combination are identified, thus flagging it for review to ensure accurate matching.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"D:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\fast_match\\coordinator.py","EndLine":572,"StartLine":520,"toolAction":"Viewing lines 520-572 of coordinator.py","toolSummary":"View lines 520-572 of coordinator.py"}}]}
